## Why This Is Asked
Offline-first reliability with service workers is a critical requirement in modern e-commerce applications. This question evaluates whether a candidate understands how to test caching behavior, connectivity state changes, and retry logic in end-to-end tests.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first UX patterns with service workers
- Network throttling and failure simulation (Cypress or Playwright network interception)
- Test data isolation with fixtures or unique identifiers
- Idempotent order placement to prevent duplicate charges

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Intercept network requests to simulate offline behavior
cy.intercept('POST', '/api/payment', (req) => {
  req.reply({ statusCode: 503, body: { error: 'Network error' } });
}).as('paymentRequest');

// Simulate going offline
cy.networkIdle(); // or use Cypress offline plugin
cy.window().then((win) => {
  win.navigator.onLine = false;
});

// Verify offline UI and localStorage persistence
cy.get('[data-testid=offline-banner]').should('be.visible');
cy.getLocalStorage('cart').should('exist');

// Restore network and retry
cy.networkOn();
cy.wait('@paymentRequest').then(() => {
  cy.get('[data-testid=order-confirmation]').should('be.visible');
});

// Verify idempotent order creation
cy.get('@paymentRequest').its('response.statusCode').should('eq', 200);
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes a beginner-friendly yet realistic E2E scenario: draft persistence, UI interactions, and end-to-end verification across multiple pages (feed and profile), with API mocking and test data isolation.

## Key Concepts

- LocalStorage persistence and autosave behavior
- End-to-end API mocking with intercept/stub
- Test data seeding and isolation
- Cross-page assertions and state verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Cypress example
describe('Drafts and Publish', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Seed test user
    cy.request('POST', '/api/test/setup', { user: 'test-user' }).then(() => {
      // Mock the publish API
      cy.intercept('POST', '/api/posts', {
        statusCode: 201,
        body: { id: '123', status: 'published' }
      }).as('publishPost');
    });
    cy.visit('/compose');
  });

  it('autosaves draft, preserves on reload, and publishes to feed and profile', () => {
    // Compose a draft
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').type('My new post draft');

    // Wait for autosave (15 seconds)
    cy.wait(15000);
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.exist;
    });

    // Reload and verify draft restoration
    cy.reload();
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').should('contain', 'My new post draft');

    // Publish the post
    cy.get('[data-testid="publish-btn"]').click();
    cy.wait('@publishPost');

    // Verify draft is cleared
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.be.null;
    });

    // Verify post appears in main feed
    cy.visit('/feed');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');

    // Verify post appears on profile
    cy.visit('/profile/test-user');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');
  });
});
```

